From 9120bc73a529057f6ed3b1e187e42344d694a630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:52:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] docs: describe the review or the machine, not session codes
 or host names

Developer notes and review records named the review sessions that measured
something (by their codes) or the workstations a measurement was made on (by
their host names). Each now says what the reader needs: "review, M2", "the
review's fixture", or the kind of machine where it matters ("a 96-thread
Linux workstation", "a workstation"). 15 edits on 12 lines in 6 files.

Cluster and platform names (Kaiju, Gadi), including where a measurement was
made on a cluster, are left as they are for now, as are local paths in
examples and review records.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
